                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "At first glance, it looks like a pretty basic life sim. Study, improve your skills, go to work, make money, buy things to reduce stress… At some point you start hacking and making money more easily. Mechanically, the game never becomes much more than that.\n\nThe strange part is that underneath this simple and slightly soulless loop, it keeps trying to tell some kind of unsettling story. Dreams, dead coworkers, increasingly bizarre events… eventually the game starts saying, “there’s something else going on here.” Did I fully understand what it was trying to say? Not really. Honestly, I’m not even sure the developer did :D But that weirdness is exactly what made it stick with me.\n\nThe mechanics are very primitive, the interface shows its age, and most of what you do is basically repeating the same few actions. Still, the game is short enough that it doesn’t overstay its welcome. The achievements can be a little annoying in places, but getting 15/15 was still pretty satisfying.\n\nIt’s hard to call this a genuinely good game. But if you like digging through old, forgotten indie games on Steam and occasionally finding something that makes you go “what the hell is this?”, it has a certain charm. I’ll probably forget most of the mechanics in a few months, but I’ll remember that uncomfortable, hard-to-define atmosphere.\n\nBadly made, but interesting. And sometimes that’s more fun than something polished that makes you feel absolutely nothing.",
